;; launchd: submitting or bootstrapping jobs (launchctl submit, bootstrap, load).
;; These go to launchd through the bootstrap port, not a named service; launchd
;; asks the caller's sandbox about `job-creation`. Shown: `(allow default)` alone
;; already refuses all three; an explicit `(allow job-creation)` opens them.
;; The explicit deny keeps the route closed whatever else the policy allows.
(deny job-creation (with message (param "SANDBOX_TAG")))
